{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Deterministic Finite-State Automaton.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Deterministic Finite-State Automaton.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"deterministic finite state automaton deterministic finite state automaton","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Deterministic Finite-State Automaton.md","fileName":"Deterministic Finite-State Automaton.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Deterministic Finite-State Automaton","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-16 22:54\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Regular Languages and Finite Automata]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Regular Languages and Finite Automata","String","FoundationsOfComputation_2.3.2.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Deterministic Finite-State Automaton.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Deterministic Finite-State Automaton.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"deterministic finite state automaton deterministic finite state automaton","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Deterministic Finite-State Automaton.md","fileName":"Deterministic Finite-State Automaton.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Deterministic Finite-State Automaton","heading":"Deterministic Finite-State Automaton","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A deterministic finite-state automaton is a five-part machine (Q, Σ, q₀, δ, F): a finite state set, input alphabet, start state, total transition function, and set of accepting states. Every state-symbol pair selects exactly one next state.\n\nThe machine accepts a [[String]] when consuming the entire string from q₀ ends in F. Its states summarize only the finite information about the processed prefix that is relevant to future acceptance.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Regular Languages and Finite Automata","String","FoundationsOfComputation_2.3.2.pdf"],"prope